==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* [[webpage]], [[web-page]]

===Etymology===
1994, {{compound|Web|page}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[web]] [[page]]}}

# A single [[hypertext]] document (transmitted as [[HTML]]) on the [[World Wide Web]], often [[hyperlink]]ed to others, and intended to be viewed with a [[web browser]].
# {{context|loosely|lang=en}} A [[website]], by extension from the [[home page]] of the site.
#* '''2007''', Doug Rich, “How to Search for Supernovae”, in ''Astronomy'', v 35, n 3 (March), pp 70–72:
#*: Dave Bishop, an amateur astronomer, operates a supernova '''web page''' at www.rochesterastronomy.org/supernova.html, which lists new discoveries, including images.

